From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Fix aborts in the PulseAudio helper during stream teardown

Stopping a cast aborted the stream process with "free(): invalid pointer".

Three separate defects combined:

 1. nd-pulseaudio.c declared a g_autofree variable directly inside a switch
    case. Its cleanup handler runs on every exit from the switch statement,
    including the PA_CONTEXT_FAILED/TERMINATED paths that jump over the
    initialisation, so glibc was handed an uninitialised pointer. Finalizing
    the object disconnects the context, which enters exactly that branch.
 2. nd-stream.c freed the NdPulseaudio object from the async init callback
    while self->pulse still referenced it, and took ownership of an object
    it did not own on success.
 3. The PulseAudio context was accessed without the threaded mainloop lock,
    and nd_pulseaudio_unload() waited on a condition that nothing signalled.

The object is now only stored once initialisation has actually succeeded and
the stream is not shutting down, every context access happens under the
mainloop lock, callbacks are detached and the mainloop is stopped before the
context is released, and the unload path is signalled by its own callback.

--- a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
+++ b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
@@ -138,6 +138,11 @@
